 What's new
-==========
-
+===
 
 .. NOTE: there are 3 separate sections for changes, based on type:
 
@@ -266,6 +265,7 @@ Bugs
 - Document in :class:`moabb.datasets.EPFLP300` that subject 3's sessions ``"0"`` and ``"1"`` store T7 and T8 as copies of the mastoid channels MA1 and MA2, so that after the mastoid reference T7 is the opposite of T8 and the 32 EEG channels have rank 31: covariance estimators without shrinkage (e.g. ``xdawn_estimator="scm"`` of ``XdawnCovariances``, as in ``pipelines/XdawnCov_MDM.yml``) fail there with a ``LinAlgError`` (:gh:`1311` by `Bruno Aristimunha`_).
 - :class:`moabb.datasets.Zhou2016` now reads its BIDS release from NEMAR (``nm000115``) under the default ``"auto"`` download provider instead of always downloading the Zenodo ``sub-N.zip`` archives: the deposit has no ``sourcedata/``, so the base class asked NEMAR for it, failed, and fell back to Zenodo on every load. The deposit holds the same EDF, ``events.tsv``, ``channels.tsv`` and ``electrodes.tsv`` files as the archives (without their ``desc-<hash>`` entity); loading subjects 1 and 2 from each source gives identical raw data, annotations, channels, epochs, labels and metadata. A subject already fetched loads without a request; ``"upstream"`` keeps the Zenodo path, and under ``"auto"`` a NEMAR failure falls back to Zenodo with a warning (:gh:`1303` by `Bruno Aristimunha`_).
 - Fix epochs of one dataset coming out with different numbers of samples when its subjects were recorded at different sampling rates and the paradigm resamples. MOABB resamples the epochs, and MNE gives ``round(n_times * new_sfreq / native_sfreq)`` samples, so a 0-3 s epoch has 601 samples at 200 Hz when it was recorded at 160 Hz (481 samples) but 602 when it was recorded at 128 Hz (385 samples), the last one at 3.005 s, after ``tmax``; any call that stacked such subjects (``get_data`` over several subjects, :class:`~moabb.evaluations.CrossSubjectEvaluation`) stopped in ``np.concatenate``. Resampled epochs now keep at most the number of samples :class:`mne.Epochs` gives for the window at the new rate (601 here), and a call whose recordings still differ by a sample (downsampling by more than a factor of two rounds the length down, e.g. 769 samples at 256 Hz give 384 at 128 Hz against 385 from 250 Hz) cuts every epoch to the shortest length; nothing is padded. Data at a single native rate are unchanged unless resampling placed samples after ``tmax`` (e.g. 128 Hz resampled to 200 Hz), which are now dropped. The resample step is part of the cache key, so cached epochs and arrays of resampled data are recomputed once (:gh:`1308` by `Bruno Aristimunha`_).
+- :class:`moabb.datasets.ErpCore2021` (all seven components) now reads its recordings from NEMAR (``nm000132``) under the default ``"auto"`` download provider instead of always downloading them from OSF: the deposit has no ``sourcedata/``, so the base class asked NEMAR for it, failed, and fell back to OSF on every load. ``nm000132`` is the ERP CORE BIDS dataset itself, one dataset whose components are the ``task-`` entity; each class now downloads its subject's files of its task (ERN and LRP share ``task-flankers``) plus the subject's ``electrodes.tsv`` and ``coordsystem.json`` into one store shared by the seven classes, ``MNE-erpcore2021-data/nm000132``. A recording already on disk, from NEMAR or from an earlier OSF download, loads without a request; ``"upstream"`` keeps the OSF path, and under ``"auto"`` a NEMAR failure falls back to OSF with a warning (:gh:`1304` by `Bruno Aristimunha`_).
 
